    {"id":"miura","cat":"berth","tier":"berth_top","priority":1,"name":"MIURA","short":"MIURA","neighborhood":"Čeladná","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=MIURA+%C4%8Celadn%C3%A1+%C4%8Cesko","badge":"MICHELIN","tags":["€ (MICHELIN price band)","Online booking via hotel site (slots 12:00-19:00) or phone","Lunch, then a walk in the Beskydy"],"productTags":["Beskydy & around"],"hours":"MICHELIN lists none; online table slots run 12:00-19:00 (hotel site). Phone before driving out.","why":"MIURA was built in 2011 by the Prague studio Labor 13 on the 7th fairway of the Čeladná golf course, and the collector's art goes all the way into the dining room: Basquiat and Daniel Arsham downstairs, Warhol's Two Gold Mona Lisas & Two White Mona Lisas and Damien Hirst above, and Petr Pastrňák's painting Nová huť, the New Steelworks, as a nod to Ostrava. MICHELIN describes a high, bright room with designer pendants and full-height windows onto the hills. Chef Michal Göth cooks Beskydy produce; Seznam Zprávy (April 2025) named the tasting menu Chuť Beskyd, Taste of the Beskydy.","address":"Čeladná 887, 739 12 Čeladná","phone":"+420 558 761 100","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.535243,"lng":18.327349,"category":"creme","subcat":"THE SERIOUS ROOMS","hook":"Bib Gourmand cooking of the Beskydy in a concrete-and-glass art hotel, eaten under Warhol and Basquiat.","person":"Michal Göth (chef)","signature":"The 'Chuť Beskyd' tasting menu","verdict":"The Beskydy's Bib Gourmand: lunch in an art gallery, then a walk in the hills; about 40 minutes' drive south of Ostrava.","caveat":"A car trip from Ostrava; MICHELIN lists no opening hours, and booking slots online run 12:00-19:00 only.","price_range":"€ (MICHELIN price band)","reservation":"Online booking via hotel site (slots 12:00-19:00) or phone","best_time":"Lunch, then a walk in the Beskydy","dishes":[{"name":"Chuť Beskyd tasting menu","note":"Beskydy-sourced tasting menu, named by Seznam Zprávy (Apr 2025); contents not published online."},{"name":"Vegetarian tasting menu","note":"Fully vegetarian set, per Seznam Zprávy (Apr 2025)."},{"name":"Regional and international classics à la carte","note":"MICHELIN describes the carte as regional and international classics."}],"signal_chip":{"label":"MICHELIN Bib Gourmand","full":"MICHELIN Guide Czechia: Bib Gourmand (selection revealed Dec 2025); Gault&Millau Česko 2025: named among the region's two top-rated restaurants","cosign":"MICHELIN Guide Czechia"},"charter":{"price":"€ (MICHELIN band)","book":"Online, slots 12:00–19:00, or phone","dress":"","warn":"Forty minutes by car from Ostrava; the last booking slot is 19:00","fit":"The region's only Bib Gourmand, under the Beskydy"},"web":"https://www.miura.cz"},
    {"id":"cattaleya","cat":"shop","tier":"several","priority":4,"name":"Cattaleya","short":"Cattaleya","neighborhood":"Villa Cattaleya, a forest-edge resort about 2.5 km from Miura","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Cattaleya+%C4%8Celadn%C3%A1+%C4%8Cesko","badge":"MICHELIN","tags":["Book direct","Lunch in daylight for the forest view"],"productTags":["Beskydy & around"],"hours":"Own site: restaurant Mon-Sat 12:00-22:00, Sun 12:00-21:00, kitchen one hour earlier. MICHELIN: closed Mon-Tue. The two disagree; phone before a Monday or Tuesday.","why":"MICHELIN describes a light, airy glass pavilion on a round floor plan beside a seven-room villa, and the kitchen reads the Czech larder like a score. The menu opens with roe deer, slivovice and mountain cheese poured with a Moravian Grüner Veltliner; bramboračka, the everyday potato soup, comes back as a mushroom consommé; fallow deer arrives with gingerbread, black salsify and berries; smoked pork with red cabbage and kluski, the Silesian word for dumplings. There is even pig's snout with smoked shallot, mustard and horseradish. The pudding is a poppy-seed dumpling with marzipan.","address":"Čeladná 510, 739 12 Čeladná","phone":"+420 734 510 006","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.540534,"lng":18.355193,"category":"creme","subcat":"THE SERIOUS ROOMS","hook":"A round glass pavilion in the Čeladná woods: venison, slivovice and Moravian Riesling on seven courses.","signature":"Fallow deer with gingerbread, black salsify and berries","verdict":"The ambitious, priced-up option of the region; worth it if the day is a Beskydy day anyway.","caveat":"Opening days conflict between MICHELIN (closed Mon-Tue) and its own site (open daily). No pets in the restaurant.","price_range":"Tasting menu 2,990 CZK; wine pairing 1,990 CZK; non-alcoholic pairing 1,090 CZK","reservation":"Book ahead by phone (+420 734 510 006) or the form on the site","best_time":"Lunch in daylight for the forest view","dishes":[{"name":"Srnčí gulášovka se slivovicí","note":"Roe deer goulash soup with slivovice, 350 CZK."},{"name":"Daněk, perník, černý kořen, bobule","note":"Fallow deer, gingerbread, black salsify, berries, 850 CZK."},{"name":"Vepřové, uzené, červené zelí, kluski","note":"Pork and smoked pork, red cabbage, kluski dumplings, 660 CZK."},{"name":"Houbové consommé à la bramboračka","note":"The potato soup rewritten as a mushroom consommé, 260 CZK."},{"name":"Vepřový rypák, uzená šalotka, hořčice, křen","note":"Pig's snout, smoked shallot, mustard, horseradish, 320 CZK."},{"name":"Candát, bisque, noky, šafrán","note":"Zander, bisque, small dumplings, saffron, 760 CZK."}],"signal_chip":{"label":"MICHELIN selected","full":"MICHELIN Guide Czechia: selected (no distinction shown); Gault&Millau Česko 2025: named among the region's two top-rated restaurants","cosign":"MICHELIN Guide Czechia"},"charter":{"price":"Tasting menu 2,990 CZK; wine pairing 1,990 CZK; non-alcoholic pairing 1,090 CZK","book":"Book ahead by phone (+420 734 510 006) or the form on the site","dress":"","warn":"Opening days conflict between MICHELIN (closed Mon-Tue) and its own site (open daily). No pets in the restaurant.","fit":"A round glass pavilion in the Čeladná woods: venison, slivovice and Moravian Riesling on seven courses."},"web":"https://www.cattaleya.cz/restaurace"},
    {"id":"hogofogo-bistro","cat":"berth","tier":"berth_top","priority":2,"name":"HogoFogo Bistro","short":"HogoFogo Bistro","neighborhood":"Ostrava","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=HogoFogo+Bistro+Ostrava","badge":"NEW WAVE","tags":["Lunch set 320 CZK; mains 298-590 CZK (menu changes weekly)","Weekday lunch"],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Mon-Fri 11:30-22:00; lunch set 11:30-15:00; closed weekends","why":"'Hogo fogo' is Czech slang for posh, and the joke is the point: this is a relaxed bistro in a historic house with a garden, a few steps off Sokolská třída. The founders still run it: Zuzka, the 'big boss' and chef who loves Sicilian pastry; Terka, head chef, a surfer and climber who admits to a weakness for fried cheese with tartar sauce; and Pítr behind the bar. They ferment, pickle and cook zero-waste, and post a dated menu every week: pumpkin gnocchi with sage and guanciale, and a vdolek, the round Czech yeast cake, to finish.","address":"Sokolská třída 871/6, 702 00 Ostrava","phone":"+420 774 854 665","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.837322,"lng":18.2938,"category":"rising","subcat":"THE NEW WAVE","hook":"Since 2015 in an old house with a garden off Sokolská: vdolek, duck rillettes and tonkotsu ramen, weekdays.","person":"Terka (head chef), Zuzka, Pítr (founder)","signature":"Vdolek and duck rillettes - old Czech pastry beside French charcuterie","verdict":"The most consistently recommended bistro in central Ostrava; a good lunch for a cook.","caveat":"Weekdays only (Mon-Fri); the Apetit piece notes it sometimes closes at weekends.","price_range":"Lunch set (soup, chicken red curry, small drink) 320 CZK; mains 298-476 CZK, US tenderloin 590 CZK per 100 g (menu changes weekly)","reservation":"Phone +420 774 854 665 or online","best_time":"Weekday lunch","dishes":[{"name":"Kachní rillettes, mandlové aioli, toust","note":"Duck rillettes, almond aioli, toast, 262 CZK."},{"name":"Tonkotsu ramen","note":"98 CZK small, 368 CZK large."},{"name":"Dýňové noky, šalvěj, guanciale","note":"Pumpkin gnocchi with sage and guanciale, 338 CZK."},{"name":"Vdolek","note":"The round Czech yeast cake, 148 CZK."}],"charter":{"price":"Lunch set (soup, chicken red curry, small drink) 320 CZK; mains 298-476 CZK, US tenderloin 590 CZK per 100 g (menu changes weekly)","book":"Phone +420 774 854 665 or online","dress":"","warn":"Weekdays only (Mon-Fri); the Apetit piece notes it sometimes closes at weekends.","fit":"Since 2015 in an old house with a garden off Sokolská: vdolek, duck rillettes and tonkotsu ramen, weekdays."},"web":"https://www.hogofogobistro.cz"},
    {"id":"stracena-garden","cat":"shop","tier":"several","priority":5,"name":"Stračena Garden","short":"Stračena Garden","neighborhood":"Svinov, next to the U Stračeny farm shop","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Stra%C4%8Dena+Garden+Ostrava","badge":"NEW WAVE","tags":["Steaks 220-900 CZK"],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Mon-Thu 11:30-21:00; Fri-Sat 11:30-22:00; Sun closed","why":"Stračena is an old Czech name for a spotted cow, and the beef here comes from the company's own farm in Klokočov: Czech Fleckvieh, the spotted český strakatý, alongside Charolais and Hereford. Rib eye, T-bone and striploin dry-age at least 60 days before they meet the Josper charcoal oven in the open kitchen; herbs come from the large garden beside the terrace. The small plates are pure Czech pub: baked tvarůžky, the ripe and pungent quark cheese of Olomouc, under bacon; pickled hermelín; and roasted back fat on onion and garlic with bread.","address":"Polanecká 56, 721 00 Ostrava-Svinov","phone":"+420 704 607 780","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.814177,"lng":18.197514,"category":"rising","subcat":"THE NEW WAVE","hook":"Steak from the family farm in Klokočov, hung 60 days and seared on a charcoal Josper, by a Svinov garden.","signature":"Czech dry-aged rib eye","verdict":"The farm-to-grill steak of Ostrava; near Svinov station.","caveat":"Closed Sundays.","price_range":"Small plates 138-153 CZK; steaks 560-900 CZK","reservation":"Phone or email (info@stracenapub.cz)","best_time":"A dry evening on the garden terrace","dishes":[{"name":"Rib eye steak","note":"Dry-aged at least 60 days, 900 CZK."},{"name":"Rozpečené tvarůžky se slaninou","note":"Baked Olomouc cheese with bacon and bread, 148 CZK."},{"name":"Pečené hřbetní sádlo na cibuli a česneku","note":"Roasted back fat on onion and garlic, bread, 138 CZK."},{"name":"Celé kuřátko z pod cihly","note":"Whole chicken under a brick, on the Josper, for four, 600 CZK."}],"charter":{"price":"Small plates 138-153 CZK; steaks 560-900 CZK","book":"Phone or email (info@stracenapub.cz)","dress":"","warn":"Closed Sundays.","fit":"Steak from the family farm in Klokočov, hung 60 days and seared on a charcoal Josper, by a Svinov garden."},"web":"https://www.stracenagarden.cz"},
    {"id":"bernie-s-grill-wine","cat":"shop","tier":"several","priority":6,"name":"Bernie's Grill & Wine","short":"Bernie's Grill & Wine","neighborhood":"Ostrava","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bernie%27s+Grill+%26+Wine+Ostrava","badge":"NEW WAVE","tags":["Recommended at weekends","Dinner"],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Mon-Sat 8:00-24:00; Sun 8:00-22:00","why":"The team came over from KORAS Restaurant and set up on the block its own site calls the street that never sleeps, Stodolní, with several rooms under one roof: the grill-and-wine restaurant, a Prosciutto Bar, an Irish pub and a wine shop. Wine is the thread. Winemakers come to pour in person: Castello di Querceto from Tuscany on 21 October 2026, the owner of Marchesi di Barolo for a six-course dinner before that. Next on the board is a Halloween prosecco evening on 30 October, with the saxophonist Radim Nowak. Doors open at 8:00, so it also works for breakfast.","address":"Poděbradova 826/27, 702 00 Ostrava","phone":"596 117 639","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.835624,"lng":18.283741,"category":"rising","subcat":"THE NEW WAVE","hook":"A grill, a wine list and a prosciutto bar under one roof on the Stodolní block, open from 8:00.","signature":"Grill plates with a serious wine list","verdict":"Central, long hours, wine-led; a safe dinner rather than a discovery.","caveat":"The site names no chef and lists no dishes or prices online; Gault&Millau toque count not confirmed (paywalled).","reservation":"Recommended at weekends","best_time":"Dinner","dishes":[{"name":"Grill steaks","note":"House concept is grill and wine; specific cuts not listed on the pages read."},{"name":"Prosciutto from its Prosciutto Bar","note":"The company runs a Prosciutto Bar alongside the restaurant."}],"signal_chip":{"label":"Maurerův výběr","full":"Maurerův výběr Grand Restaurant (selection listed)","cosign":"Maurerův výběr Grand Restaurant"},"charter":{"price":"Grill plates; serious wine list","book":"Recommended at weekends","dress":"","warn":"","fit":"Open from 8:00 to midnight Mon–Sat, to 22:00 Sunday"},"web":"https://www.bernies.cz"},
    {"id":"harenda-u-barborky","cat":"berth","tier":"berth_top","priority":3,"name":"Harenda U Barborky","short":"Harenda U Barborky","neighborhood":"Petřkovice, inside the Landek Park mining museum grounds","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Harenda+U+Barborky+Ostrava","badge":"CZECH","tags":["3-course tasting menu 695 CZK","Phone","Lunch after the Landek mine tour"],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Wed-Thu 11:30-20:00; Fri-Sat 11:30-22:00; Sun 11:30-20:00","why":"Harenda sits in a historic brick building inside Landek Park, which CzechTourism describes as the canteen where the miners used to eat. The motto of owner-chef Adam Cakl is 'hezky, česky, moderně': nicely, Czech, modern. This autumn the three-course menu runs from chicken terrine with pistachio, prunes and black-garlic mayonnaise to roe deer shoulder in rosehip sauce with an orange-zest herb dumpling and lardo, then semolina foam with plums and gingerbread. From 6 to 17 November comes the St Martin's feast: goose leg, red and white cabbage, lokše potato flatbreads, bread dumpling and goose gravy.","address":"Pod Landekem 68, 725 29 Ostrava-Petřkovice","phone":"723 977 506","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.868177,"lng":18.264243,"category":"houses","subcat":"THE CZECH KITCHEN","hook":"The old miners' canteen at Landek, now cooking Czech 'hezky, česky, moderně'; goose from 6 November.","person":"Adam Cakl (owner, chef)","signature":"St Martin's goose with red and white cabbage, lokše and dumpling (6-17 Nov)","verdict":"The one table that puts you on Ostrava's mining ground; go for the mine, stay for the goose.","caveat":"Closed Monday and Tuesday. The feast dates carry no year on the site (footer © 2025): confirm by phone.","price_range":"3-course tasting menu 695 CZK","reservation":"Phone","best_time":"Lunch after the Landek mine tour","dishes":[{"name":"Roe deer shoulder, rosehip sauce, herb dumpling with orange zest, lardo","note":"Course of the 3-course tasting menu (695 CZK)."},{"name":"Chicken terrine with pistachio, prunes, black-garlic mayo","note":"Tasting-menu starter."},{"name":"Semolina foam with plums and gingerbread","note":"Tasting-menu dessert."},{"name":"Roast goose with lokše","note":"St Martin's feast, 6-17 Nov (year not printed)."}],"charter":{"price":"3-course tasting menu 695 CZK","book":"Phone","dress":"","warn":"Closed Monday and Tuesday. The feast dates carry no year on the site (footer © 2025): confirm by phone.","fit":"The old miners' canteen at Landek, now cooking Czech 'hezky, česky, moderně'; goose from 6 November."},"web":"https://www.harenda.cz","hot_this_month":"November 2026: the St Martin's goose with lokše, 6–17 November (confirm by phone)."},
    {"id":"u-jarosu","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":7,"name":"U Jarošů","short":"U Jarošů","neighborhood":"Poruba, Pustkovecká","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=U+Jaro%C5%A1%C5%AF+Ostrava","badge":"CZECH","tags":[],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Mon 10:45-22:00; Tue-Fri 10:45-23:00; Sat 11:00-23:00; Sun 11:00-22:00","why":"Until 1989 this corner of Pustkovecká was the butcher's shop of Jaroš Křibek, and people came from far around for his meat and stayed to talk. So his son and son-in-law rebuilt the shop as a restaurant, the house says, so that customers could stay longer. The butcher's counter is gone, but the cooking keeps to good meat: Czech classics 'in a modern coat', with tasting menus built to order for a table. On 7 October 2026 the kitchen announced this year's husí hody, the goose feast, under the line 'A zase ta husička', the goose again.","address":"Pustkovecká 138, 708 00 Ostrava-Poruba","phone":"+420 596 925 524","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.840259,"lng":18.157166,"category":"houses","subcat":"THE CZECH KITCHEN","hook":"Poruba's famous butcher's shop became a restaurant: Czech cooking 'in a modern coat', and goose now.","signature":"Autumn goose feast (husí hody)","verdict":"A neighbourhood house with a butcher's lineage; worth it in goose season.","caveat":"Out in Poruba, 20+ minutes by tram from the centre.","reservation":"Phone +420 596 925 524 or ujarosu@seznam.cz","best_time":"Goose season, October to November","dishes":[{"name":"Husí hody","note":"Goose feast, announced 7 Oct 2026."},{"name":"Tasting menus to order","note":"Multi-course menus built on request."}],"signal_chip":{"label":"Maurerův výběr","full":"Maurerův výběr Grand Restaurant (selection listed)","cosign":"Maurerův výběr Grand Restaurant"},"charter":{"price":"","book":"Phone +420 596 925 524 or ujarosu@seznam.cz","dress":"","warn":"Out in Poruba, 20+ minutes by tram from the centre.","fit":"Poruba's famous butcher's shop became a restaurant: Czech cooking 'in a modern coat', and goose now."},"web":"https://www.ujarosu.cz","hot_this_month":"Autumn 2026: goose feasts, announced 7 October."},
    {"id":"stara-kuzelna","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":8,"name":"Stará kuželna","short":"Stará kuželna","neighborhood":"Ostrava","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Star%C3%A1+ku%C5%BEelna+Ostrava","badge":"CZECH","tags":["Mains 249-339 CZK"],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Mon-Fri 11:00-22:00; Sat 12:00-22:00; Sun 12:00-20:00; Fri 23 Oct 2026 open from 17:00 only","why":"Kuželna is a skittle alley, and the name promises an old-style Czech pub; behind it is a large house, listed with 200 seats and a summer garden, and a kitchen that posts a careful weekly menu. In the week of 19 October 2026 that meant dršťková, the peppery tripe soup; smoked beef tongue with horseradish sauce and house dumpling; Hungarian perkelt with tarhoňa, the egg-barley pasta; grilled calf's liver with bacon and jalapeño mayonnaise. On Friday 23 October the band Skrat launch their record here from 17:00, entry free.","address":"","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.837487,"lng":18.301902,"category":"houses","subcat":"THE CZECH KITCHEN","hook":"Old skittle-alley house with 200 seats and a garden: tripe soup, smoked tongue, perkelt, and a gig on Friday.","signature":"Smoked beef tongue with horseradish sauce","verdict":"A real kitchen behind a pub-style room; check the address before setting out.","caveat":"Address is not printed on its own site; the city tourism list gives Na Baranovci 5.","price_range":"Mains 249-339 CZK","dishes":[{"name":"Dršťková polévka","note":"Tripe soup, 79 CZK."},{"name":"Uzený hovězí jazyk, křenová omáčka, domácí knedlík","note":"Smoked beef tongue, horseradish sauce, house dumpling, 249 CZK."},{"name":"Maďarský perkelt, tarhoňa","note":"With sour cream, 269 CZK."},{"name":"Grilovaná telecí játra","note":"Grilled calf's liver, fries, bacon, jalapeño mayo, 269 CZK."}],"signal_chip":{"label":"Maurerův výběr","full":"Maurerův výběr Grand Restaurant (selection listed)","cosign":"Maurerův výběr Grand Restaurant"},"web":"https://stara-kuzelna.cz"},
    {"id":"ostrawica-lokal","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":9,"name":"Ostrawica Lokál","short":"Ostrawica Lokál","neighborhood":"Ostrava","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ostrawica+Lok%C3%A1l+Ostrava","badge":"LUNCH","tags":["Lunch 179-249 CZK","Weekday lunch"],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Mon-Thu 8:00-22:30; Fri 8:00-23:00; Sat 8:00-22:30; Sun 10:00-21:00; breakfast Mon-Sat 8:00-10:00; lunch 11:00-15:00","why":"Ostrawica writes the river's name the old way, with a w, and cooks the shared table of the Czech and Austrian lands as mothers and grandmothers made it: schnitzel, strong broth, goulash, roštěná, apple strudel, desserts made in the house. The weekday lunch is posted by date. On Wednesday 21 October 2026 it was svatební svíčková, the wedding version of the Sunday beef in cream-and-root-vegetable sauce, with a cranberry topping and two kinds of bread dumpling, for 195 CZK; the soup is bottomless at 35 CZK. Staropramen on tap, a glass of mineral water free with lunch.","address":"Solná 1, Ostrava","phone":"+420 593 033 029","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.836183,"lng":18.29217,"category":"cantine","subcat":"POLEDNÍ MENU","hook":"The river's old spelling over the door, 'wedding' svíčková on the plate, and soup refilled for 35 CZK.","signature":"Svíčková with cranberries and dumplings","verdict":"The easiest honest lunch in the centre.","caveat":"Staropramen on tap, not a local beer.","price_range":"Lunch 179-249 CZK","best_time":"Weekday lunch","dishes":[{"name":"Svatební svíčková na smetaně","note":"Wedding svíčková, cranberries, two kinds of dumpling, 195 CZK."},{"name":"Pečený pstruh po mlynářsku","note":"Miller's-style trout, crushed chive potatoes, salted tomatoes, 249 CZK."},{"name":"Bezedná polévka","note":"Bottomless soup of the day, 35 CZK."}],"charter":{"price":"Lunch 179–249 CZK","book":"Walk in; lunch from 11:00","dress":"","warn":"Staropramen on tap, not a local beer","fit":"On the main square, open every day, to 22:30 most nights"},"web":"https://www.ostrawica.cz"},
    {"id":"burfi","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":10,"name":"Burfi","short":"Burfi","neighborhood":"Ostrava","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Burfi+Ostrava","badge":"LUNCH","tags":["Full menu 129 CZK (19-23 Oct, year not printed)"],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Mon-Fri 11:00-14:00","why":"Burfi first opened in 2005 and came back as a vegan and vegetarian takeaway bistro with one idea: a single daily menu, cooked from fresh produce, no shortcuts. For 129 CZK the week of 19 October brought mung-bean soup, sabji with jasmine rice, kofta in a tomato-chutney sauce, a coconut curry with green beans on Friday, a salad, and every day a square of sweet halva. Soup comes with Burfi's own bread balls. The kitchen serves 11:00 to 14:00 on weekdays, and delivers within 8 km Monday to Thursday.","address":"Přívozská 134/6, 702 00 Moravská Ostrava","phone":"+420 774 402 179","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.837227,"lng":18.290628,"category":"cantine","subcat":"POLEDNÍ MENU","hook":"Vegetarian since 2005: one Indian-leaning set a day, sweet halva included, 129 CZK, three hours only.","person":"Keshava Kempe (operator)","signature":"Daily set with sweet halva","verdict":"Cheapest honest lunch in the centre; three hours a day only.","caveat":"Mon-Fri 11:00-14:00 only.","price_range":"Full menu 129 CZK (19-23 Oct, year not printed)","dishes":[{"name":"Kofty s rajskou čatny omáčkou a rýží","note":"Kofta in tomato-chutney sauce with rice, in the 129 CZK set (Thu, week of 19 Oct)."},{"name":"Brokolicové sabdži s rýží","note":"Broccoli sabji with rice, in the set (Wed, week of 19 Oct)."},{"name":"Sladká halva","note":"Comes with every daily set."}],"web":"https://burfi.net"},
    {"id":"los-dobrotos","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":11,"name":"Los Dobrotos","short":"Los Dobrotos","neighborhood":"Ostrava","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Los+Dobrotos+Ostrava","badge":"LUNCH","tags":[],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Mon 10:00-19:00; Tue-Thu 10:00-21:00; Fri 10:00-22:00 (the site itself marks Friday with a question mark); Sat 11:00-21:00; Sun closed","why":"'Dobroty' is Czech for treats; give it a Spanish article and you have the name. The counter on Velká smells of churros fried to order, and the rest is Spain in a box: tapas boxes of jamón, chorizo and Spanish cheese, crisps (truffle ones too), Estrella beer, Spanish wines and specialty coffee. At lunch it feeds the University of Ostrava: students with an ISIC or university card get the daily menu with a Kofola for 135 CZK. Paella is cooked to order for events.","address":"Velká 198/14, 702 00 Ostrava","phone":"+420 603 995 329","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.834527,"lng":18.291709,"category":"cantine","subcat":"POLEDNÍ MENU","hook":"A Spanish street-food counter on Velká: churros fried fresh, jamón-and-chorizo boxes, a student lunch.","person":"Daniel Ryška (manager)","signature":"Fresh churros","verdict":"Cheap, cheerful, central; churros as the reason.","caveat":"Lunch menu posted as images only.","dishes":[{"name":"Churros","note":"Fried fresh."},{"name":"Tapas box","note":"Jamón, chorizo, Spanish cheese."},{"name":"Daily lunch menu","note":"135 CZK with Kofola for University of Ostrava students."}],"web":"https://www.losdobrotos.cz"},
    {"id":"happy-banh-mi","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":12,"name":"Happy Banh Mi","short":"Happy Banh Mi","neighborhood":"Masarykovo náměstí","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Happy+Banh+Mi+Ostrava","badge":"ELSEWHERE","tags":[],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Mon-Fri 10:30-20:00; Sat-Sun 11:30-16:30","why":"A family bistro that brought, in its own words, a piece of Vietnam to Ostrava, and has reopened its branch on Masarykovo náměstí. The baguette that names it comes with house pâté and pork, chicken or beef. The bowls cover the country: phở bò from the north, cooked or rare; bún bò Huế, the chilli-hot beef noodle soup of the old imperial city, with Vietnamese ham; bún bò Nam Bộ, the southern beef noodle salad with peanuts and fried shallots; and bún chả lá lốt, minced pork grilled in betel leaves. How the Vietnamese came to Czech cities is told elsewhere in this guide.","address":"Masarykovo nám. 24/13, Moravská Ostrava","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.836131,"lng":18.293204,"category":"ethnic","subcat":"THE OTHER KITCHENS","hook":"Family Vietnamese bistro on the main square: bánh mì with house pâté, phở bò, and pork in betel leaves.","signature":"Phở bò","verdict":"The pho stop in the centre.","caveat":"Aggregator reviews are mixed beyond the bánh mì.","dishes":[{"name":"Bánh mì","note":"With house pâté; original, pork, chicken or beef, 155 CZK."},{"name":"Phở bò chín/tái","note":"Beef pho, cooked or rare, 205 CZK."},{"name":"Bún bò Huế","note":"Spicy Huế beef soup with Vietnamese ham, 225 CZK."},{"name":"Bún chả lá lốt","note":"Minced pork in betel leaves with rice noodles, 210 CZK."}],"web":"https://www.happybanhmi.cz"},
    {"id":"pelmeski","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":13,"name":"Pelmeški","short":"Pelmeški","neighborhood":"Ostrava","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Pelme%C5%A1ki+Ostrava","badge":"ELSEWHERE","tags":[],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Mon-Fri 10:30-19:30; Sat-Sun 12:00-19:00","why":"Pelmeški has filled dumplings by hand since 2018, the Russian pelmeni and the Ukrainian vareniky, a thousand ways: meat, vegetarian, sweet. The first order is the potato vareniky, under fried onion and a fistful of dill, parsley and spring onion; the house twist is pork-and-kimchi pelmeni with sesame and chilli. To drink there is Wostok, the half-forgotten Soviet 'Bajkal' herbal lemonade, revived a few years ago by a Berliner. The bestsellers are frozen in kilo bags, so dinner can travel home.","address":"Českobratrská 113/22, 702 00 Ostrava","phone":"+420 775 473 132","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.838839,"lng":18.286461,"category":"ethnic","subcat":"THE OTHER KITCHENS","hook":"Pelmeni and vareniky since 2018, a revived Soviet herbal lemonade, and kilo bags in the freezer.","person":"Martin Štubňa (operator)","signature":"Potato vareniky","verdict":"A quick, filling eastern-European lunch near the centre.","best_time":"Order ahead for a set time to skip the queue","dishes":[{"name":"Vareniky bramborové","note":"Potato vareniky with fried onion and herbs, small 155 CZK."},{"name":"Pelmeně Asian Fusion","note":"Pork with kimchi, about 300 g, 225 CZK."},{"name":"Pelmeně kuřecí","note":"Chicken, parmesan, basil, about 300 g, 215 CZK."}],"web":"https://www.pelmeski.cz"},
    {"id":"gokana","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":14,"name":"Gokana","short":"Gokana","neighborhood":"Ostrava","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Gokana+Ostrava","badge":"ELSEWHERE","tags":[],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"","why":"Gokana is a sushi house with a cook's shop attached: alongside the rolls it sells Japanese knives in Damascus steel, a 25 cm blade among them. The sushi side does yellowfin tuna tartare with avocado guacamole and elaborate California rolls such as the Dragon, wrapped in seared river eel with kabayaki sauce. Moss Bistro, its ramen corner, runs a weekday lunch: a bao bun with shrimp popcorn, then red curry or chicken paitan ramen, with house lemonade. The Gokana lunch set for 19–23 October 2026 was 299 CZK.","address":"Zámecká 1666/17, 702 00 Ostrava","phone":"+420 720 588 588","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.834641,"lng":18.29006,"category":"ethnic","subcat":"THE OTHER KITCHENS","hook":"Sushi house that also sells Damascus-steel Japanese knives, with Moss Bistro's ramen and bao on the side.","signature":"Yellowfin tuna tartare","verdict":"The reference sushi in the city.","caveat":"Delivery-led site; closes 19:30 on the day read.","dishes":[{"name":"Yellowfin tuna tatar","note":"With avocado guacamole and bread, 315 CZK."},{"name":"Dragon roll","note":"Tempura shrimp, river eel, kabayaki, 429 CZK for 6 pieces."},{"name":"Moss lunch menu","note":"Bao bun, then red curry or paitan ramen, lemonade, 249-279 CZK."},{"name":"Gokana lunch set","note":"Endoshoto, shiitake hosomaki, salmon nigiri, 299 CZK, 19-23 Oct 2026."}],"signal_chip":{"label":"Maurerův výběr","full":"Maurerův výběr Grand Restaurant (selection listed)","cosign":"Maurerův výběr Grand Restaurant"},"web":"https://www.gokana.cz"},
    {"id":"cokafe","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":15,"name":"CØKAFE Dolní Vítkovice","short":"CØKAFE Dolní Vítkovice","neighborhood":"Dolní Vítkovice","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=C%C3%98KAFE+Doln%C3%AD+V%C3%ADtkovice+Ostrava","badge":"COFFEE","tags":[],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Listed on Wolt: weekdays 08:00-18:00, weekends 08:00-19:00","why":"Seznam Zprávy put CØKAFE's largest branch at the heart of Dolní Vítkovice, in a building that once served the steelworks, and singled out its industrial atmosphere; in summer there is a large garden. The coffee comes from the owners' own roastery and the cakes from their own patisserie and bakery, so breakfast here is the house's own from cup to crumb: on Wolt in October 2026, eggs Benedict 224 CZK, a flat white 99 CZK, a lemon bar 88 CZK. Who now owns the chain is told elsewhere in this guide.","address":"Vitkovicka 3369, Moravská Ostrava","phone":"+420 775 496 266","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.821794,"lng":18.27777,"category":"coffee","subcat":"COFFEE","hook":"Ostrava's own coffee chain at its largest branch, in a former steelworks building at Dolní Vítkovice.","person":"Richard Mauler (founder)","signature":"House-roasted espresso with a pastry from its own bakery","verdict":"The best-located coffee in the city: breakfast here, then the blast furnace next door.","caveat":"Hours known only from Wolt (weekdays 8:00-18:00, weekends 8:00-19:00); the chain's own site did not load.","dishes":[{"name":"Eggs Benedict","note":"224 CZK."},{"name":"Flat white","note":"99 CZK, house roast."},{"name":"Lemon bar","note":"88 CZK, own patisserie."}]},
    {"id":"laura-coffee","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":16,"name":"Laura Coffee","short":"Laura Coffee","neighborhood":"Ostrava","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Laura+Coffee+Ostrava","badge":"COFFEE","tags":[],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"","why":"Laura Coffee began in 2012 with a love of food, cooking and coffee in the family, roasting in the attic of the family house, and took its name from the elder daughter, Laura. It now roasts for dozens of cafés, hotels and restaurants, bakes its own bread and cakes, teaches latte art, and runs five cafés, two of them inside Ostrava Zoo. The one to know is the smallest: kafeKostka, a kiosk at Ostrava-Svinov station, open every day since 2014 from early morning, so the first cup of the trip can be a good espresso or batch brew.","address":"Horni 1492/55, 700 30 Ostrava-Hrabůvka (company seat)","phone":"+420 770 160 602","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.821241,"lng":18.208981,"category":"coffee","subcat":"COFFEE","hook":"A family roastery begun in an attic in 2012; its smallest café is the kiosk at Svinov station.","person":"Ivo Ptáčník (founder)","signature":"Espresso or batch brew at the Svinov kiosk","verdict":"The coffee to grab at Svinov when you arrive by train.","caveat":"Kiosk hours are not published ('from early morning'); the other cafés are out of the old centre.","dishes":[{"name":"V60 / batch brew","note":"at kafeHrabůvka"},{"name":"House bread and cakes","note":"from its own bakery"}],"web":"https://lauracoffee.cz"},
    {"id":"shothouse-ostrava","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":17,"name":"Shothouse Ostrava","short":"Shothouse Ostrava","neighborhood":"Nádražní, city centre","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Shothouse+Ostrava+Ostrava","badge":"COFFEE","tags":["Table booking online"],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Mon-Thu 08:00-21:00, Fri 08:00-23:00, Sat 09:00-21:00, Sun 09:00-12:00","why":"Shothouse grew up in Havířov, next door, and now runs bars there and on Nádražní in Ostrava. It treats coffee as something to learn: it sells cupping sessions, where you taste coffees side by side the way roasters judge them, and Huskee cups made from the husk, the parchment layer stripped from the bean. A 2025 coffee guide noted two batch-brew options on the bar and laptops welcome when it is quiet. Street brunch at the table, booked online in seconds; on Fridays the bar stays open until 23:00.","address":"Nádražní 756/49, Ostrava","phone":"+420 737 016 243","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.83818,"lng":18.284682,"category":"coffee","subcat":"COFFEE","hook":"A Havířov coffee bar on Nádražní: batch brew, cupping sessions and cups made from coffee husk.","signature":"Batch brew","verdict":"A good laptop morning in the centre.","caveat":"Sunday hours are short (09:00-12:00).","reservation":"Table booking online","dishes":[{"name":"Filter / batch brew","note":"two options daily"},{"name":"Street brunch","note":"listed on its own site"}],"web":"https://www.shothouse.cz"},
    {"id":"elektra","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":18,"name":"Kavárna Elektra","short":"Kavárna Elektra","neighborhood":"Nádražní, city centre","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kav%C3%A1rna+Elektra+Ostrava","badge":"COFFEE","tags":["Mains 249-287 CZK (menu changes weekly)","Breakfast 07:00-10:00"],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Mon-Fri 07:00-19:00","why":"The Elektra palace was built in 1924–26 as the Miners' House, paid for by the miners' trade union to designs by Kubíček, Kolář and Rubý, and its café was the workers' grand room. It went dark for twelve years until J&T Banka reopened it in 2012, restored by the Brno architect Petr Hrůša: a 25-metre ceiling relief of folded gold petals, a bar of white glass, terrazzo set with white marble pebbles, and op-art panels of plum, rosewood, merbau and pear. The week of 19 October 2026 was Austro-Hungarian: Fiakergulasch of fallow deer with egg and pickle, 269 CZK.","address":"Nádražní 305/5, 702 00 Ostrava","phone":"+420 221 710 842","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.834171,"lng":18.28789,"category":"coffee","subcat":"COFFEE","hook":"The Miners' House café of 1924–26, reopened by J&T Banka under a 25-metre ceiling of gold petals.","signature":"Breakfast under the gold ceiling","verdict":"Ostrava's one proper grand-cafe room; go for breakfast or the lunch menu.","caveat":"Weekdays only; closes 19:00, lunch menu served to 18:00.","price_range":"Mains 249-287 CZK (menu changes weekly)","best_time":"Breakfast 07:00-10:00","dishes":[{"name":"Croissant Benedikt","note":"House croissant, Špejlík smoked meat, poached eggs, hollandaise, 239 CZK."},{"name":"Wiener Schnitzel","note":"Veal, 287 CZK."},{"name":"Wiener Fiakergulasch","note":"Fallow-deer goulash, sausage, fried egg, pickle, Viennese dumpling, 269 CZK."},{"name":"Reisauflauf","note":"Baked rice, port-soaked plums, vanilla cream, meringue, 236 CZK."}],"web":"https://ostrava.jtbankacafe.cz"},
    {"id":"drinkeat","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":19,"name":"Drinkeat","short":"Drinkeat","neighborhood":"Ostrava","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Drinkeat+Ostrava","badge":"BREAKFAST","tags":["Online","Weekend morning"],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Mon-Thu 7:30-18:00; Fri 7:30-22:00; Sat-Sun 8:00-14:00","why":"Drinkeat is a brunch bistro run by two women, Barča and Kačka, and the address the Ostrava promoter Jan Petrus gave Apetit in March 2026 when asked where to brunch. Inside there is a corner of armchairs and a small private room; in summer, an overgrown garden in the courtyard where the street noise drops away. The coffee is roasted for them by Nordbeans in Liberec, and the drinks card changes every month. Order the Turkish eggs, or roast beef on bread under a fried egg; kefir pancakes for the sweet side.","address":"Poděbradova 312/32, 702 00 Moravská Ostrava a Přívoz","phone":"+420 728 200 920","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.836122,"lng":18.283845,"category":"breakfast","subcat":"BREAKFAST & BRUNCH","hook":"Brunch room on Poděbradova: Turkish eggs, Nordbeans coffee, an armchair corner and an overgrown courtyard.","person":"Barbora Šindlerová (Barča) and Kačka","signature":"Turkish eggs","verdict":"The breakfast to send a crew to.","caveat":"Weekend hours only to 14:00.","reservation":"Online or by phone","best_time":"Weekend morning","dishes":[{"name":"Turkish eggs","note":"Per Apetit (Mar 2026)."},{"name":"Eggs Benedict","note":"Per Apetit."},{"name":"Roast beef on bread with a fried egg","note":"Per Apetit."},{"name":"Kefir pancakes","note":"Per Apetit."}],"web":"https://drinkeat.cz"},
    {"id":"lajka-zije","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":20,"name":"Lajka žije","short":"Lajka žije","neighborhood":"'U Sýkoráku' (by the Miloš Sýkora bridge)","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Lajka+%C5%BEije+Ostrava","badge":"BREAKFAST","tags":[],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Mon-Fri 8:00-18:00; Sat 9:00-17:00; Sun 9:00-15:00","why":"The name means 'Laika lives', and the café's tagline says she still does, 'u Sýkoráku', by the Miloš Sýkora bridge. Seznam Zprávy called it playful: a roomy espresso bar where you can sit, with coffee from the DAK roastery, lemonade and matcha, and a second-hand corner selling vintage clothes, accessories, books and records. Breakfasts follow the season. Dogs and cyclists are welcome by policy, and it is walk-in only, so arrive early on a weekend.","address":"","phone":"732 420 328","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.837242,"lng":18.295259,"category":"breakfast","subcat":"BREAKFAST & BRUNCH","hook":"'Laika lives' by the Sýkora bridge: DAK coffee, matcha, seasonal breakfasts and a rail of vintage clothes.","signature":"Seasonal breakfast","verdict":"Coffee-and-eggs stop on the way to Slezská Ostrava.","caveat":"Walk-in only. Street address not printed on its own site; coffee directories give 28. října 572/4.","dishes":[{"name":"Seasonal breakfast","note":"Breakfast menu PDF, 2026/08 upload."},{"name":"Specialty coffee and matcha","note":"Own site."}],"web":"https://www.lajkazije.cz"},
    {"id":"zamek-zabreh","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":21,"name":"Zámek Zábřeh — Pivovar Pikard","short":"Zámek Zábřeh","neighborhood":"Zábřeh","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Z%C3%A1mek+Z%C3%A1b%C5%99eh+Pivovar+Pikard+Ostrava","badge":"BREWERY","tags":["Table booking on the website"],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Not published on its own site; book a table online or by phone.","why":"Zábřeh began as a Gothic water fort and became a Renaissance chateau around 1600; it reopened in 2007 as a hotel with two restaurants and its own brewery. A gallery and corridor hung with hunting trophies lead to the old rooms, a brick-and-beam stair to the attic. The house beer is Pikard, unfiltered, unpasteurised, with an 11° pale lager always on. The kitchen keeps a calendar: pig-killing feast, Easter lamb and kid, summer asparagus and mushrooms, St Martin's goose, winter game; the brewers follow with a spring nettle beer and a Christmas ginger beer.","address":"U Zamku 42/1, 700 30 Ostrava-Zábřeh","phone":"+420 777 808 299","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.807085,"lng":18.240266,"category":"brewery","subcat":"BEER","hook":"A chateau in Zábřeh with its own brewery: unfiltered Pikard, trophy halls and a vaulted beer-bath cellar.","signature":"House lager poured in the chateau brewery restaurant","verdict":"The most atmospheric place in the city to drink beer brewed on the premises.","caveat":"Out of the centre (Zábřeh, south Ostrava); the beer spa is a gimmick you can skip.","reservation":"Table booking on the website","dishes":[{"name":"Seasonal beer specials","note":"from spring nettle beer to Christmas ginger beer"},{"name":"Martinmas goose","note":"part of the chateau's seasonal kitchen calendar, which also runs to winter game"}],"web":"https://www.zamek-zabreh.cz"},
    {"id":"hermanicky-pivovar","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":22,"name":"Heřmanický pivovar","short":"Heřmanický pivovar","neighborhood":"Ostrava","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=He%C5%99manick%C3%BD+pivovar+Ostrava","badge":"BREWERY","tags":["Essential at weekends"],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Brewery listed weekdays 13:00-17:00 on Slevomat; restaurant hours not confirmed","why":"Heřmanický pivovar brews unfiltered, unpasteurised beer from Czech raw materials on Vrbická street in Heřmanice. The tour is small and personal: reviewers from August to 15 October 2026 praise the owner's explanations and the food, a smoked pork knuckle among it, though one wanted a wider beer list. Afterwards the restaurant Beseda next door pours the house beers on tap, with a garden and the party piece, metr piva, ten half-litres lined up on a board. Weekend tour slots were reported full to the end of 2026: book a weekday.","address":"Vrbická 614/131, Ostrava-Slezská Ostrava","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.85925,"lng":18.330007,"category":"brewery","subcat":"BEER","hook":"Small brewery in Heřmanice: the owner shows you the tanks, then lunch next door at Beseda.","signature":"House lager from the tank","verdict":"Book a weekday tour; this is where Ostrava's small-brewery scene actually lives.","caveat":"No own website found; trading confirmed only through a deal-site listing with reviews dated up to 15 Oct 2026.","price_range":"Tour with tasting and food, 1-2 people, 699 CZK on Slevomat","reservation":"By phone at least two days ahead (number on the voucher listing); weekends booked to year-end","dishes":[{"name":"Brewery tour with tasting","note":"booked weeks ahead at weekends"},{"name":"Metr piva","note":"ten 0.5 l beers on a board, for a group"}]},
    {"id":"radegast","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":23,"name":"Pivovar Radegast, Nošovice","short":"Pivovar Radegast, Nošovice","neighborhood":"Beskydy foothills, 30 km south of Ostrava","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Pivovar+Radegast%2C+No%C5%A1ovice+No%C5%A1ovice+%C4%8Cesko","badge":"BREWERY","tags":["Book ahead: exkurze@radegast.cz","Weekday or Saturday afternoon"],"productTags":["Beskydy & around"],"hours":"Visitor centre listed Mon-Sat 10:00-17:00 (Apr-Sep), 10:00-16:00 (Oct-Mar); Czech-language tours listed Tue and Sat 14:00","why":"Few breweries make bitterness their slogan. Radegast's own site greets you with 'Život je hořký. Bohudík!', Life is bitter. Thank God!, and the beer keeps the promise: a firmly hopped Moravian lager. At the brewery you can go past the tour into Radegastova škola čepování, the tapping school, where the lesson is the Czech pour, foam and all. In late 2025 it also ran evening tours by headlamp with a longer tasting. The god on the label stands on the Radhošť ridge (see the Pustevny walk); the tower tasting is in Autour.","address":"Nošovice 238, 739 51 Nošovice","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.661251,"lng":18.427241,"category":"brewery","subcat":"BEER","hook":"Radegast at Nošovice sells bitterness as a creed: 'Life is bitter. Thank God!' Learn to tap it there.","signature":"A tasting in the observation-tower restaurant","verdict":"The easiest serious brewery tour from Ostrava; pair it with a Beskydy day.","caveat":"No 2026 tour prices or times found: the Kudy z nudy figures are undated, and the 2025 evening tours cost 250 CZK. Book through exkurze@radegast.cz or +420 558 602 566.","price_range":"Tour listed 250 CZK adult, 180 CZK reduced, 650 CZK family","reservation":"exkurze@radegast.cz or +420 558 602 566 (tour desk, per Kudy z nudy)","best_time":"Weekday or Saturday afternoon","dishes":[{"name":"Tour tasting","note":"poured in the tower restaurant at the end of the tour"},{"name":"Radegastova škola čepování","note":"tapping school, listed at 650 CZK"}],"web":"https://www.radegast.cz"},
    {"id":"u-zrzave-mary","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":24,"name":"U Zrzavé Mary","short":"U Zrzavé Mary","neighborhood":"Ostrava","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=U+Zrzav%C3%A9+Mary+Ostrava","badge":"PUB","tags":[],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"","why":"'U Zrzavé Mary' means 'At Red-haired Mary's', and the room keeps to the colour: dark-red walls, brooding light, wooden tables, antiques piled on antiques and old wireless radios stacked high along the walls. The European Bar Guide calls it a cult pub and dive bar, lists it among its Top 100 Bars in Europe for 2026, and describes the scene at the grim-looking entrance, regulars smoking outside, a younger crowd within. Draught comes from small independent breweries; the back bar is good; pizza is the food.","address":"Jurečkova 12, Moravská Ostrava","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.834444,"lng":18.28711,"category":"pub","subcat":"THE HOSPODA","hook":"Red-haired Mary's: dark-red walls, old wireless sets stacked to the ceiling, smokers at the door.","signature":"Independent draught beer, late","verdict":"The late beer after the gig, not the first one.","caveat":"Dark, smoky-at-the-door dive; hours and phone not published.","dishes":[{"name":"Small-brewery draught","note":"modest rotating range"},{"name":"Back-bar spirits","note":"decent selection"}]},
    {"id":"kurnik-sopa","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":25,"name":"Kurník šopa","short":"Kurník šopa","neighborhood":"Ostrava","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kurn%C3%ADk+%C5%A1opa+Ostrava","badge":"PUB","tags":[],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Myslbekova (centre): daily 14:00-23:00; Poruba original, Pavlouskova 24: Sun-Thu 15:00-23:00, Fri-Sat 16:00-01:00","why":"Kurník šopa has poured from eight fast-rotating taps since September 2012, small and medium Czech breweries and some foreign ones, and every keg it taps gets its own beer sheet pinned up for you to read. The European Bar Guide found one room stretched around a long bar, mid-brown furniture, retro signs, and staff and regulars moving like a ballet. On 20 October 2026 the board ran from a 10° Olbrew from Sedlnice through Šopák, a fresh-hop 11° lager, to a Rauchbier and a 14° West Coast IPA. Over 70 rums; a women's beer circle.","address":"Myslbekova 13, Ostrava","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.849939,"lng":18.279877,"category":"pub","subcat":"THE HOSPODA","hook":"Eight rotating taps since 2012, a beer sheet pinned up for every keg, and 70 rums behind the bar.","signature":"Rotating independent lagers","verdict":"Where Ostrava's beer people drink when they want something other than the big three.","caveat":"The original Kurník šopa is a basement pub in Poruba, Pavlouskova 24.","reservation":"Phone recommended, it fills up","dishes":[{"name":"Guest lagers","note":"usually unfiltered and unpasteurised"},{"name":"Bottle list","note":"some other European beers"}]},
    {"id":"hokuspokus","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":26,"name":"HokusPokus","short":"HokusPokus","neighborhood":"Škroupova, city centre","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=HokusPokus+Ostrava","badge":"WINE","tags":[],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Site footer: Tue-Thu 16:00-23:00, Fri 16:00-00:00, Sat 18:00-00:00, Sun-Mon closed. The Ostrava contact box lists Thu-Sat only: check before a Tuesday or Wednesday.","why":"The owners spent twenty years on prize-winning conventional wine until it bored them, they say; they wanted wines 'without life and full of chemistry' off their list. Now every bottle is organic or natural, from growers across Europe they know personally, and the growers come to the bar: in 2026 Partida Creus and Microbio on 13 May, Jean-François Ganevat's Jura wines on 14 May, and on 3 June the Špetík family, Moravian natural winemakers, pouring orange wines. Eat house sourdough with pâté from Melememaso, Spanish ham and French cheese.","address":"Škroupova 1114/4, Ostrava","phone":"+420 778 799 456","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.836276,"lng":18.285509,"category":"wine-bar","subcat":"WINE","hook":"Natural wine on Škroupova, sister of the Prague bar, with growers who come in person to pour.","signature":"Natural wine by the glass","verdict":"The best glass of wine in the city; Moravian bottles share the list with European natural growers.","caveat":"Closed Sunday and Monday; not a Moravian-only list.","dishes":[{"name":"Wine by the glass","note":"Organic and natural only."},{"name":"Sourdough bread with pâté","note":"House-baked bread, hand-made pâté from Melememaso."},{"name":"Spanish ham and French cheese","note":"Own site."}],"web":"https://hokuspokus.cz"},
    {"id":"winestone","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":27,"name":"Winestone","short":"Winestone","neighborhood":"Českobratrská, city centre","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Winestone+Ostrava","badge":"WINE","tags":[],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Business lunch Mon-Fri 11:30-14:00","why":"The name is two English words, and the stone is literal: dishes come out on slate boards the house calls 'les planches'. Every dish on the à la carte menu is matched to a glass from the list, and the hotel's own page promises food and wine 'served in a creative way' in a designed room. On weekdays there is a business lunch from 11:30 to 14:00 and a weekly lunch menu. It is a calm hotel dining room rather than a destination, a block from Stodolní.","address":"Českobratrská 1742/18, Ostrava","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.839323,"lng":18.28818,"category":"wine-bar","subcat":"WINE","hook":"The Mercure's ground-floor wine restaurant: every dish matched to a glass, served on slate boards.","signature":"Dish-and-glass pairing","verdict":"A safe hotel option for a glass with dinner, not a destination.","caveat":"Moravian focus not confirmed; menus are linked from the hotel site only.","dishes":[{"name":"Business lunch","note":"Mon-Fri 11:30-14:00"},{"name":"Wine pairing","note":"glass chosen per dish"}]},
    {"id":"nox","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":28,"name":"NOX — Provoz","short":"NOX","neighborhood":"Ostrava","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=NOX+Provoz+Kosteln%C3%AD+24+Ostrava","badge":"LATE","tags":["Gig entry 250-350 CZK"],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Mon-Sat from 16:00; Mon-Thu to 00:00, Fri-Sat to 02:00","why":"NOX is the bar of Provoz, a cultural centre on the Ostravice embankment within sight of the Sýkora bridge, and it pours, in its own words, good drink beside concerts, vinyl and books. The same collective runs the Inverze literary festival, the Luft audiovisual festival, the Harakiri platform and the publisher Bílý Vigvam. The club room holds 100 standing or 80 seated. On the autumn 2026 board: Market and Laokoon on 24 October, the Barevná továrna record launch on 6 November, Power for Ukraine with Krang on 13 November.","address":"Kostelní 24, 702 00 Ostrava","phone":"+420 604 748 376","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.836608,"lng":18.295858,"category":"late-night","subcat":"AFTER DARK","hook":"The Provoz collective's bar: records, books and a 100-standing gig room, open till 2 at weekends.","person":"Tomas Homolik (bar manager, programmer)","signature":"A drink and whatever is on the turntable","verdict":"The closest thing Ostrava has to a listening bar: records, books and a serious gig room.","caveat":"Not a hi-fi bar in the Japanese sense; gigs carry a door charge (250-350 CZK).","price_range":"Gig entry 250-350 CZK","dishes":[{"name":"Bar drinks","note":"beer, wine, spirits"},{"name":"Vinyl and books","note":"sold over the bar"}],"web":"https://www.provoz.net/nox","hot_this_month":"November 2026: a record launch on 6 November, Power for Ukraine on 13 November."},
    {"id":"heligonka","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":29,"name":"Heligonka","short":"Heligonka","neighborhood":"Dolní Vítkovice","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Heligonka+Ostrava","badge":"LATE","tags":["Tickets ahead"],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Open on concert days only, 18:00-21:00","why":"A heligonka is the button accordion of Moravian folk music, and the club's founding note, signed by Jarek Nohavica and Pavel Giertl in September 2015, reads like a song: here the high sky touches the hard ground, couplets are sung beside opera arias, the engineer sits at one round table with the shop assistant, and coffee is drunk in the shadow of the blast furnaces because the shift is over. The room is non-smoking and no photos during shows.","address":"Vitkovicka 42/3367, 702 00 Ostrava","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.822498,"lng":18.278116,"category":"late-night","subcat":"AFTER DARK","hook":"Nohavica's own cabaret club under the furnaces, where 'the engineer shares a table with the shop assistant'.","person":"Jaromír Nohavica, Pavel Giertel","signature":"A Nohavica evening","verdict":"Book a night Nohavica plays; it is Ostrava's songwriter in his own room.","caveat":"Coming by tram: the underpass at Dolní Vítkovice, Hlubina is closed for building works; use the Dolní Vítkovice stop and walk through the site.","price_range":"Varies by night; tickets on heligonka.cz","reservation":"Tickets ahead","dishes":[{"name":"Bar","note":"drinks with the show"},{"name":"Concert","note":"the reason to go"}],"web":"https://www.heligonka.cz"},
    {"id":"dock","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":30,"name":"Dock","short":"Dock","neighborhood":"Havlíčkovo nábřeží, Malá Kodaň (river embankment)","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Dock+Ostrava","badge":"LATE","tags":["Phone only"],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Mon 14:00-23:00, Tue-Thu 08:00-23:00, Fri 08:00-00:00, Sat 09:00-00:00, Sun 09:00-22:00","why":"Dock calls itself 'above all an informal space': a café and bistro by day, a bar by night where you sit or stand, and often a bit of culture. The rules are part of the charm. You order and pay at the tap, the right moment to buy a friend a round; tables are booked by phone only and the place never closes for private parties; drinks to go leave only in 50 CZK deposit cups, paid in cash. Weekend breakfast, 9:00 to 12:00, is the one time staff serve the tables. On 27 October 2026 the Provoz collective takes over the room.","address":"Havlíčkovo nábřeží 28, Ostrava","phone":"+420 603 335 791 (reservations)","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.836532,"lng":18.296065,"category":"late-night","subcat":"AFTER DARK","hook":"Café by day, bar and small music club by night on the Ostravice embankment; order at the tap.","signature":"Beer, wine or a cocktail on the river terrace","verdict":"The best single bar in Malá Kodaň, where Ostrava now goes out.","caveat":"Bring cash for cup deposits.","reservation":"Phone only","dishes":[{"name":"Weekend breakfast","note":"09:00-12:00, table service only then"},{"name":"Bistro plates","note":"afternoons"}],"web":"https://www.clubdock.cz"},
    {"id":"folk-food","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":31,"name":"Folk Food","short":"Folk Food","neighborhood":"Poruba, Čkalovova","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Folk+Food+Ostrava","badge":"STREET","tags":[],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Tue-Sun 11:00-22:00, orders to 21:30","why":"Folk Food is three men from Ostrava with more than fifty years in kitchens between them, from washing dishes to running their own catering, who chose the hot dog because it can be done averagely or properly. They make the sausages to their own recipe, smoke the meat and pickle the vegetables in-house, and take bread fresh each morning from a local bakery. The Chilli Folk dog comes with pickled white cabbage, plum barbecue sauce, chipotle and jalapeño; the pulled-pork Folk roll with plum BBQ and crackling.","address":"Čkalovova 6144/18, Ostrava-Poruba","phone":"+420 731 407 330","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.82991,"lng":18.175942,"category":"street","subcat":"LA RUE","hook":"Three Ostrava cooks rebuild the párek v rohlíku: own sausage, own smokehouse, morning brioche.","signature":"Chilli Folk dog with sauerkraut and plum BBQ","verdict":"Fast, local, made in-house.","caveat":"Closed Mondays; site footer © 2025.","dishes":[{"name":"Chilli Folk dog","note":"150 g sausage, pickled cabbage, plum BBQ, chipotle, jalapeño, 169 CZK."},{"name":"Cheddar Folk dog","note":"Cheddar sauce, onion-bacon jam, 179 CZK."},{"name":"Folk roll s trhaným vepřovým","note":"Pulled pork, plum BBQ, crackling, 159 CZK."},{"name":"Naše uzená Gouda","note":"House-smoked gouda, 150 g, 159 CZK."}],"web":"https://folkfood.cz"},
    {"id":"faency-fries","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":32,"name":"FÆNCY FRIES","short":"FÆNCY FRIES","neighborhood":"Vítkovice, Ruská","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=F%C3%86NCY+FRIES+Ostrava","badge":"STREET","tags":[],"productTags":["Ostrava"],"hours":"Daily 10:00-20:00","why":"FÆNCY FRIES starts in the field: the potatoes are Czech, grown in the Beskydy foothills or on the Vysočina, the variety tested before it reaches the fryer, with a 'potato of the week'. The method is Flemish, fried twice, first long and low, then short and hot, in neutral vegetable oil, finished with Alpine salt; the dips are made to house recipes. The cone was redesigned so the top fries do not drown in the dip. The Æ is a pun: fancy, or 'Do you fancy fries?'. Order cheddar dip with bacon.","address":"Čs. legií 1719/5, Moravská Ostrava (per visitostrava)","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-10-21","lat":49.836865,"lng":18.289849,"category":"street","subcat":"LA RUE","hook":"Fries cut from Beskydy or Vysočina potatoes, fried twice the Flemish way, in a cone built for dipping.","signature":"Fries with cheddar dip and bacon","verdict":"A cheap hot snack on the walk through the centre; second counter in Poruba, Hlavní třída 72.","caveat":"Closes at 20:00, so not a late-night stop; prices not on the site.","dishes":[{"name":"Fries with cheddar dip and bacon","note":"Own site."},{"name":"Fries with mayonnaise and red onion","note":"Own site."}],"web":"https://faencyfries.cz"}
